# The old address in production serves only the moved page (vite.site.config.ts, MC_SITE=moved). Netlify reads these
# before netlify.toml, so links into the old site that have a page of their own at the new address go straight there;
# every other path falls through to netlify.toml's catch-all and shows the moved page, which has to stay on this origin
# to read the saves it holds. The MarvelCDB proxy in netlify.toml keeps answering for apps that still call it.
/releases/*            https://play.champions-digital-game.com/releases/:splat    301
/sync-info.html        https://play.champions-digital-game.com/sync-info.html     301
/shadowland-info.html  https://play.champions-digital-game.com/releases/           301
